## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the ability to design per-tenant traffic control across data centers, implement dynamic configuration updates, and establish observability—all without service downtime.

## Key Concepts
- **Deterministic hashing**: Ensures consistent per-tenant canary decisions across all service instances
- **Docker Config**: Enables dynamic configuration reloads and zero-downtime rollouts
- **Multi-DC routing**: Traefik handles TLS termination with per-tenant observability across both data centers

## Code Example
```javascript
function isCanary(tenant, percentage) {
  const hash = [...tenant].reduce((acc, char) => (acc * 31 + char.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0, 0);
  return (hash % 100) < percentage;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to add observability with OpenTelemetry in a docker-dca context, ensuring end-to-end trace propagation from edge to service and basic validation.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry instrumentation and OTLP exporter
- otel-collector as a sidecar and Jaeger backend
- Trace context propagation (traceparent/tracestate)
- docker-compose scaffolding for api, nginx, collector
- Basic end-to-end validation via Jaeger UI

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js OpenTelemetry setup (simplified)
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/tracing');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider();
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(
  new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: 'http://otel-collector:4318/v1/traces' })
));
provider.register();
```

